Requirements: 6   with obligations: 6

[task-01] When they finish, the benchmark's command-line runs — the instability
    measurement and the mutant audit — print the per-stage usage table that `acceptance
    check` and `acceptance decompose` already print, with live and replayed calls
    counted apart, so a large offline run shows what it cost.
    -> benchmark-cli-prints-usage-table  [functional/explicit, code_and_tests]
       When the benchmark's command-line runs (the instability measurement and the
       mutant audit) finish, each prints the same per-stage usage table that `acceptance
       check` and `acceptance decompose` already print.
    -> usage-table-live-replayed-counted-apart  [functional/explicit, code_and_tests]
       In the per-stage usage table printed by the benchmark's command-line runs (the
       instability measurement and the mutant audit), live model calls and replayed
       calls are counted in separate figures, so that the two are never combined into a
       single count.
    -> offline-run-usage-cost-visible  [explanation_observability/explicit, code_and_tests]
       The usage table printed by the benchmark's command-line runs reports the cost of
       a large offline run, so that a reader of the output can see what the run cost.

[task-02] The table shows what the run spent on Claude models separately from what it
    spent on any other provider, so the Claude credits a run consumed can be read off as
    a figure of its own. A call sent through the Message Batches API counts at the price
    it was billed at.
    -> claude-spend-separate-figure  [functional/explicit, code_and_tests]
       The table presents the run's spend on Claude models as a figure separate from the
       run's spend on any other provider, so the Claude credits consumed by a run can be
       read off as its own figure.
    -> batch-call-counted-at-billed-price  [functional/explicit, code_and_tests]
       A call sent through the Message Batches API is counted in the run's spend at the
       price it was billed at (the batch price), not at the standard non-batch price for
       the same model.

[task-03] Spend stays out of the review state and the rendered report, as it is today.
